{number: 39}
{title: There Shall Be Showers of Blessing}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] There shall be showers of blessing:
This is the [F7] promise of love;
There shall be [Bb] seasons refreshing,
[F7] Sent from the Savior a-[Bb] bove.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Bb] Showers of blessing,
Showers of blessing we [F7] need:
[Bb] Mercy drops 'round us are [Eb] falling,
But for the [Bb] showers we [F7] plead. [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] There shall be showers of blessing
Precious re-[F7] viving again;
Over the [Bb] hills and the valleys,
[F7] Sound of abundance of [Bb] rain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] There shall be showers of blessing;
Send them up-[F7] on us, O Lord;
Grant to us [Bb] now a refreshing,
[F7] Come, and now honor Thy [Bb] Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Bb] There shall be showers of blessing:
Oh, that to-[F7] day they might fall,
Now as to [Bb] God we’re confessing,
[F7] Now as on Jesus we [Bb] call!
{end_of_verse}
